# Manual Content Mode

When the CTO provides complete file content for a path, Cursor must:

## Write behavior

- Write each file to the exact path given
- Overwrite the file with the supplied content
- Preserve all newlines and line breaks from the source
- Do not rewrite, summarize, or paraphrase the content
- Do not compress multiple lines into one line
- Do not optimize, refactor, or reformat unless explicitly asked

## Forbidden in this mode

- Merging partial edits when a full file was supplied
- Converting Markdown, Python, or MDC files to single-line form
- Dropping blank lines that were in the supplied content

## After writes

- Run the project format check when the task specifies it
- Run python -m pytest when Python files were written or changed
- Report which paths were written and test results
